quadrf (1.0.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ethernet direct-connect follows eth0 carrier and drops a leftover
    DHCP lease so unplug/replug starts 10.55.1.1 instead of staying in
    LAN mode.
  * Desktop mDNS names are registered on the interface that owns each
    address so nss-mdns does not return usb0 or the AP address on the LAN.
  * RF Vision Interleave enables all four channels on startup.

 -- QuadRF Engineering <contact@ScaleRF.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:29:55 -0700

quadrf (1.0.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * nginx serves the control panel at / and KasmVNC at /VNC/ (and
    desktop.HOSTNAME.local). /GUI/ redirects to /.
  * Control panel Applications panel starts/stops Spatial RF Vision, the
    camera decoder and the PSD plot through quadrf-app, which stops other
    exclusive CSI/DSI users first.
  * Network Setup can set the fallback AP SSID and WPA2 passphrase.
  * QUADRF_HOSTNAME is the mDNS/nginx name so several units on one LAN can
    be given distinct names later.

 -- QuadRF Engineering <contact@ScaleRF.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0700

quadrf (1.0.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * KasmVNC session keeps GRC Qt windows on DISPLAY :1. dbus-launch now
    execs the session so the bus survives; Qt/SDL/GTK are forced onto X11
    so HDMI/vc4 KMS does not steal the framebuffer.
  * quadrf-desktop depends on dbus-x11, wmctrl, x11-utils and
    x11-xserver-utils (xev/xrandr/wmctrl were invoked without packages).
  * Seed QRadioLink with Soapy MIPI (driver=mipi, RX/TX, 4 Msps, 8192-pt
    FFT). Rewrite leftover Pluto and ZMQ thin-client (driver=quadrf)
    device args on apply.
  * GRC File Open bookmark for /usr/share/quadrf/grc; Openbox raises
    generated python3 Qt windows.

 -- QuadRF Engineering <contact@ScaleRF.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:54:00 -0700

quadrf (1.0.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild for Debian Trixie / DietPi. qradiolink and KasmVNC now match
    Trixie library SONAMEs so apt install quadrf works on a current Pi 5.

 -- QuadRF Engineering <contact@ScaleRF.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:28:00 -0700

quadrf (1.0.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * First public release: Debian packages for the QuadRF appliance on
    Raspberry Pi 5, published via GitHub Actions to
    https://scalerf.github.io/QuadRF/
  * Metapackages quadrf and quadrf-headless, plus quadrf-common, -boot,
    -fpga, -fpga-dkms, -soapy, -gui, -network, -demos, -desktop,
    -gnuradio and -ups.
  * Signed apt repository; factory FPGA bitstream is not included.

 -- QuadRF Engineering <contact@ScaleRF.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:40:00 -0700
